<figure id="S4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.08519v1/avsync.png" id="S4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/197;" width="476" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="S4.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative comparison for audio-visual sync task.<span id="S4.F6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> For the I2V-based methods, we use the first frame generated by MoCha <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> as the input start frame. For HunyuanCustom and Ours, the cropped face from the start frame is utilized as input. The official OmniHuman-1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> website API does not support text input. Zoom in for details.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
